  {
   "fid": "2026-12-04-dustin-pague-vs-mike-richman",
   "c": "bkfc",
   "mood": "Bold prediction",
   "h": "Richman Sees Pague Fight Ending In Stoppage Or Decision",
   "sum": "Mike Richman is torn on how his main event with Dustin Pague ends, and says a win won't bring him the belt.",
   "tags": [
    "Mike Richman",
    "Dustin Pague",
    "Julian Lane"
   ],
   "q": "He's either going to get uh TKOed or KO'ed or it's going to be a decision.",
   "who": "Mike Richman",
   "ctx": "Interview with Knuckles2Knives",
   "ev": "PAGUE VS RICHMAN",
   "body": [
    "Mike Richman says his December 4 main event with welterweight champ Dustin Pague will end in a stoppage or a decision, and he admits he can't pick between them. He calls Pague “a tough cat” who can take punishment.",
    "If the shots don't finish Pague, Richman says it could turn into a repeat of Pague's last fight with Julian Lane, with both men trading for five rounds and leaving it to the judges.",
    "Richman also explained the stakes. The fight is not necessarily a title bout, and it is set at a 168-pound catch weight, which he says is closer to welterweight than middleweight. Even without the belt, he says “I know there's value in beating him”, pointing to a big fight, a good payday and a possible shot at a world title.",
    "Why it matters: Richman is fighting the champ without a title on the line, so a win only helps if it earns him a number one contender fight or a shot at 175. His own prediction suggests Pague will be hard to put away."
   ],
